WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.172 --> 00:00:07.642
How the engine finds a real vulnerability across files.

2
00:00:07.642 --> 00:00:14.646
Scan: the value is tracked from its source, through a function call, to the database call it reaches.

3
00:00:14.646 --> 00:00:21.653
Each step of the trace names its kind, file and line: source, cross-file parameter, sink.

4
00:00:21.653 --> 00:00:28.670
Side by side: the concatenated query, and the parameterised one.

5
00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:35.674
Rescanning the fixed code: the SQL text no longer carries request data, so there is nothing to report.

6
00:00:35.674 --> 00:00:42.676
A sanitizer clears only what it neutralises. Python sample: request data echoed into HTML.

7
00:00:42.676 --> 00:00:49.682
Escaping the value for HTML clears the XSS finding.
